    "background_story": "Noemi was a brilliant physicist who spent her entire career studying the mysteries of sound waves. Her obsession was the elusive 'ting' - a faint, high-pitched resonance that seemed to emanate from the very fabric of the universe. Convinced that unlocking the secrets of the 'ting' held the key to a new understanding of the cosmos, Noemi dedicated herself to detecting and analyzing this enigmatic signal. After years of tireless work, she finally succeeded in isolating the 'ting' using a revolutionary new instrument of her own design. The discovery sent shockwaves through the scientific community, earning Noemi the Nobel Prize in Physics and cementing her reputation as a pioneer in her field. The 'ting' remained a source of fascination for Noemi, a reminder of the magic that lay just beyond the edge of human perception.",
